  "note": "The 23 key families of the vanilla text sweep (spec section 3): which installed English localisation files each one sweeps, who writes it, whether its text is drawn with a country in scope (the people modifier is allowed only then), and how strictly the scan gates it. gate: off = no data yet, the scan only measures; report = ZIN text is scanned for banned words and the rest is measured; banned = additionally fails on a reachable key that still shows a vanilla value holding an error-class banned word; strict = fails on every reachable key that is neither replaced, structural, neutral nor owned elsewhere. A family moves to the next gate when its author marks it so.",
